---
source: crates/surfaces/cli/tests/read_views.rs
expression: "normalized_text(&run.stdout, root)"
---
behavior (@specforge/software): A testable unit of system functionality with a defined contract

Fields:
  abstract  bool  -  Marks a specification-only behavior that concrete behaviors refine; it carries no verify obligations of its own
  category  identifier  -  Classification tag for agent task routing
  consumes  reference_list  -  Events this behavior reacts to
  contract  string  *  The behavioral contract this behavior guarantees
  description  string  -  Human-readable summary of this behavior
  diagnostic  identifier  -  Diagnostic message for validation tooling
  ensures  block  -  Named postconditions: each condition's name and what it guarantees
  features  reference_list  -  Product features this behavior implements
  invariants  reference_list  -  Invariants this behavior enforces
  maintains  block  -  Named frame conditions that hold throughout execution
  ports  reference_list  -  Port interfaces this behavior interacts with
  produces  reference_list  -  Events produced as a result of this behavior
  refines  reference  -  Abstract behavior this concrete behavior refines; its ensures conditions must be kept (E031)
  refs  string_list  -  External references such as issue or document URIs
  requires  block  -  Named preconditions: each condition's name and what it requires
  satisfies  reference_list  -  Temporal properties this behavior satisfies
  severity  identifier  -  Impact level if this behavior fails
  status  identifier  -  Current lifecycle status of this behavior
  sync  block  -  Synchronization bound: barrier, timeout or delivery
  types  reference_list  -  Type definitions used by this behavior
Existing: login, logout, reset_password
Guide:
  Look for public functions in service, handler, or controller layers that represent user-visible operations or business logic. Route handlers (HTTP, gRPC, CLI commands), use-case functions, and domain service methods are strong signals. Map function name to entity ID (snake_case). Extract doc comments or the function's purpose as the contract. If the function validates rules or enforces constraints, those are invariants. If it emits events or messages, those are produces. If it has dedicated test files or test functions, add verify statements. Skip: private helpers, utility functions, test fixtures, generated code, framework boilerplate.
Example:
  behavior example_behavior "Example Title" {
    contract "..."
    abstract true
    category word
    consumes [ref_1, ref_2]
  }
